.TH TGATES 1 "2026-08-16" "notcoreutils" "notcoreutils Manual"
.SH NAME
tgates \- real ternary logic gates (min/max/neg/diff)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tgates neg
\fITRIT\fR[,\fITRIT\fR...]
.br
.B tgates min\fR|\fBmax\fR|\fBdiff
\fITRIT\fR[,\fITRIT\fR...] \fITRIT\fR[,\fITRIT\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tgates
computes the standard Kleene/Lukasiewicz three\-valued\-logic gates
over balanced ternary values (each \fITRIT\fR is \-1, 0, or 1). It is
the CLI half of this project's own
.B tenary_gates.h
(src/singlefile/tenary/) \- same relationship
.BR units (1)
has to its own conversion tables.
.PP
A single \fITRIT\fR or a comma\-separated list (the array/bulk form)
both work; \fBmin\fR/\fBmax\fR/\fBdiff\fR require both operand lists to
be the same length.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B neg \fITRIT\fR
Ternary NOT: negation (\-\fITRIT\fR).
.TP
.B min \fITRIT\fR \fITRIT\fR
Ternary AND: the lesser of the two values.
.TP
.B max \fITRIT\fR \fITRIT\fR
Ternary OR: the greater of the two values.
.TP
.B diff \fITRIT\fR \fITRIT\fR
Three\-way compare: \-1 if the first is less, 0 if equal, 1 if greater
(the sign of their difference, saturated back into a single trit).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR units (1)
